<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # The Importance of Panama in Global Trade – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Panama's Role in the World</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> The Importance of Panama in Global Trade</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write analytical reports on current topics like social trends or global events. Interactive: Produce a collaborative story on local or global interest topics.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write analytical reports on the Panama Canal's effects, comparing revenue statistics and environmental findings (e.g., "Since the expansion, the Canal has increased annual profits by three billion dollars but has also reduced water levels in surrounding lakes.") Can collaborate on writing a story about Panama's global impact, discussing its role in trade (e.g., "Panama has always played an important role in global trade, thanks to the Panama Canal. If Panama invested more in its infrastructure, it could become an even more powerful trade hub in the future.") Can work with classmates to outline a report on Panama's trade role, discussing key aspects like economic growth (e.g., "Let's include sections on shipping routes and local job creation.")</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher projects an image of a container ship navigating the Panama Canal. Students are asked to quickly jot down three sentences describing what they see and its potential impact on global trade. This activates prior knowledge and sets a writing context using key vocabulary like "shipping," "trade," and "impact."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes two example sentences on the board related to the image, demonstrating the target grammar (e.g., "The Canal *has been improving* global trade for over a century." and "If Panama *had not built* the Canal, global trade *would have faced* significant challenges."). The teacher orally models the pronunciation of multisyllabic words like "environmental" /ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.təl/ and "impactful" /ɪmˈpækt.fəl/, emphasizing the alternation of full and reduced vowels, and the long vowel sound /oʊ/ in "global" and "show." Students repeat.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What type of impact does 'has been improving' refer to – something finished or something ongoing?" (Expected: Ongoing.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In the sentence 'If Panama had not built the Canal...', did Panama build it or not?" (Expected: Yes, they did.)</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Panama's Role in the World".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short analytical report excerpt (approx. 150 words) on "The Environmental Impact and Economic Benefits of the Expanded Panama Canal." The text uses passive voice (e.g., "The Canal *has been managed* by the Panama Canal Authority since 1999."), second/third conditionals (e.g., "If water levels *were* consistently lower, *shipping routes would be* adjusted."), and Present Perfect Continuous (e.g., "Environmental groups *have been raising concerns* about the Canal's operations."). It includes target vocabulary like "efficiency," "investments," "ecosystems," and "sustainable."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> The student can understand the main ideas and some specific details of clear, standard written texts on topics related to the Panama Canal's role in global trade.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the excerpt silently.
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What are the two main aspects of the Panama Canal's impact discussed in the report?" (Expected: Economic benefits and environmental impact.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match phrases describing Canal benefits with phrases describing environmental concerns based on the text. For example, "Increased annual profits" (benefit) with "Reduced water levels" (concern).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar identification:</b> Students identify and underline all sentences in the text that use passive voice, a conditional structure, or the Present Perfect Continuous.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing sentences accurately using passive voice, second and third conditionals, and Present Perfect Continuous, incorporating vocabulary related to "The Importance of Panama in Global Trade." Pragmatic: Expressing hypothetical ideas and discussing the Canal's impact. Sociolinguistic: Using specific trade-related terms appropriately.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides sentence stems or cloze sentences for students to complete, focusing on the target grammar.
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The new shipping routes ___________ (monitor) carefully since last year." (Passive voice, Present Perfect Continuous)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If the government ___________ (invest) more in infrastructure, congestion ___________ (prevent)." (Second conditional)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Global trade ___________ (affect) significantly if the Canal ___________ (not complete) in the early 20th century." (Third conditional)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Panama's influence on global relationships ___________ (enhance) through its role in trade." (Passive voice)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Transformation):</b> Students work individually to rewrite active sentences into passive voice, or change factual statements into conditional statements.
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 1: "The authority oversees the Canal's operations." → "The Canal's operations ____________________ by the authority." (Passive voice)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 2: "Panama's strategic location contributes to global trade." → "If Panama ____________________ a strategic location, global trade ____________________." (Second conditional)</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 3: "Many countries have been investing in the Canal's efficiency." → "The Canal's efficiency ____________________ by many countries." (Present Perfect Continuous + Passive voice)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction / Peer Check:</b> Students exchange their completed sentences from activity 2 with a partner. They check each other's work for grammatical accuracy, correct vocabulary use, and spelling, giving constructive feedback. They then discuss which sentences best express hypothetical ideas related to the Canal. (e.g., "Your conditional sentence about investments is very clear. It uses 'invested' and 'would be prevented' correctly.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Panama's Role in the World".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Writing of an Analytical Report Paragraph.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in pairs to write a paragraph (80-100 words) for an analytical report titled "Panama Canal: A Two-Sided Coin of Progress and Challenge." The paragraph should focus on either the economic impact or the environmental concerns, comparing statistics or findings (as per learning outcome), and must include at least one example of passive voice, one conditional (second or third), and one instance of the Present Perfect Continuous. They should use a minimum of five vocabulary words from the list (e.g., "revenue," "environmental groups," "ecosystems," "investments," "influence").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The task connects directly to the theme by requiring students to analyze and report on "The Importance of Panama in Global Trade" and its associated benefits and challenges. Students will first outline key points (e.g., "Let's include sections on shipping routes and local job creation" or "We need to discuss environmental concerns that have been raised") before drafting their paragraph.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their collaboratively written paragraph from Stage 4.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher):</b> The teacher uses an observation checklist focusing on:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of passive voice (1-2 instances).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of second/third conditional (1 instance).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of Present Perfect Continuous (1 instance).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (at least 5 words).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of ideas related to the theme.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Completion of the writing task (80-100 words, analytical report style).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on an index card:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new grammar structure you successfully used in your paragraph today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one challenge you still face when writing about complex topics like global trade?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has practicing these grammar structures helped you to express more complex ideas about Panama's global role in your writing?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific feedback from your partner or the teacher will you apply to improve your next written task?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> Most students successfully incorporated passive voice and Present Perfect Continuous, but some struggled with the correct formation of third conditionals, particularly in balancing hypothetical past actions with past consequences. The collaborative writing task allowed for peer support and encouraged the use of academic vocabulary. I will provide a quick review of conditional structures at the beginning of the next lesson and consider giving sentence starters for third conditionals if students are still struggling. The explicit focus on pronunciation of multisyllabic words helped reinforce spelling for writing. Students showed good understanding of the sociolinguistic aspect by using respectful and appropriate trade terms.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration), students will summarize their written findings and present them, integrating all four skills, and consolidate their understanding of Panama's importance in global trade through a larger 21st-century skills project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>